From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:51:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/smmstore: Reclaim the variable store in SMM while a
 lock is armed

With the option lock or the MOR lock armed, the payload cannot reclaim
the variable store: its fault tolerant write erases the store and copies
it back from the spare blocks, and the locks refuse both (an erase leaves
a store without the options, a write past the store is the bypass that
the store end check closed). Every write then appends a record until the
next boot, the writes slow down with the dead records, and a full store
fails the writes of the OS.

Add SMMSTORE_RECLAIM and SMMSTORE_CMD_RECLAIM. The payload writes the
reclaimed store into a staging area, the store_end bytes before the last
block of the region, with raw writes, which a lock allows there while
armed. On COMMIT the handler reads the image back from the flash, checks
the headers, walks it, and asks each lock whether the image keeps what it
holds: the set of the options (or the security options) and the MOR
request. It then writes a commit record with the SHA-256 of the image
into the last block, which raw writes may not touch while armed, copies
the image over the store, reads it back and erases the record. Ramstage
finds a record left by a power loss before the payload and finishes the
copy from the staging area, or drops a record whose image does not match;
it takes the layout from the record, since the store's own header may be
erased. At most four reclaims a boot, and none while the store is more
than a quarter free. The swap takes one SMI: split over several, a half
written store would meet an S3 resume or another write between them.

TEST=Unit tests: the layout, the areas, the limits, a commit, an image
refused by the locks or unreadable or with other headers, the limit per
boot, a power loss after each flash operation of the commit followed by
the recovery, records with a wrong image or layout, and the image rules
of the option lock with and without SMMSTORE_OPTION_LOCK_ALL.
---
 src/drivers/smmstore/Kconfig          |  16 ++
 src/drivers/smmstore/Makefile.mk      |   2 +
 src/drivers/smmstore/mor_lock.c       |  12 +
 src/drivers/smmstore/options_lock.c   |  56 ++++
 src/drivers/smmstore/reclaim.c        | 369 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c            |  13 +
 src/drivers/smmstore/store.c          |  34 +++
 src/include/smmstore.h                |  76 +++++
 tests/drivers/Makefile.mk             |  20 ++
 tests/drivers/smmstore_options_lock.c | 134 +++++++++
 tests/drivers/smmstore_reclaim.c      | 382 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 11 files changed, 1114 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/drivers/smmstore/reclaim.c
